{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795399147,"nonce":"9twfXQn4racWnSp78kH0khb5yks=","title":"Calendar month turn: the two structural frames are most of the turn's CPU","message":"After 89538a4f (SVG pages on rows) and 19daa138 (probe waits for on_ready), a continuous month turn in `cn_demo_costs` paints every frame on rows except the structural frames: 12 turns give 121 rows frames and 23 full frames, about 2 structural frames per turn (the new month page is inserted, the leaving one removed).\n\nProfile: xctrace Time Profiler, 1 ms samples, release-debug, 80 turns (`COSTS_NO_TRACE=1 COSTS_CALENDAR=80 COSTS_CALENDAR_PHASE=turn COSTS_CALENDAR_FRAMES=12 COSTS_CALENDAR_DT=8 COSTS_ASYNC=1`), at 57a32d64. The turn loop is 1221 main-thread samples, about 15 ms per turn.\n\nStructural update (`apply_queued_updates`, 538 samples, about 6.7 ms per turn):\n- `reconcile_region` 197: `collect_render_props_boxed` 37, `apply_base_rules_to_nodes` 32, `apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides_for_subtree` 19, `remove_subtree_nodes` 15, `compute_element_tree` 13, `set_dynamic_class` 12, `later_content_overlaps_any` 11, `mint_stable_ids_under` 8.\n- `compute_layout` 110 (whole tree).\n- `apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides_scoped` 56.\n- `compute_animated_render_bounds` 42, `later_content_overlaps_any` 19, `apply_flip_transitions` 14, `start_all_css_animations` 13.\n\nFull paint of the structural frames (`render_tree_frame`, 426 samples, about 5.3 ms per turn):\n- `RenderTree::render_frame` 180: `render_layer_with_motion` 131 (`visible_children` 30, `children_qualify` 22), `plan_cross_stream_groups` 49.\n- `collect_elements_recursive` 75, `prepare_motion_text` 38, `prepare_captured_text_at` 33, `render_frame_content` 24.\n\nOther per-turn cost outside the structural frames: hit testing on scroll and mouse move, 168 samples (`hit_candidates` 83), and the GPU passes of every frame (render pass begin/end and encoder creation).\n\nSo the structural update plus its full paint is about 964 of 1221 samples. Two directions, not exclusive:\n1. Incremental paint for a structural frame whose change is inside one bound subtree: walk only that subtree and splice its primitives, collected text and records into the cached batch. Takes the paint walk, collection and text preparation (about 326 samples), but the batch ranges, binding records and CSS records after the splice all shift.\n2. Scope the update: layout of the changed region's subtree instead of the whole tree, and cheaper reconcile (render props, base rules) for 42 new cells.","files":null}]}